Title: VAULT FOURTEEN
Author: Daniel Crowe
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. ART MUSEUM - CLOSED GALLERY - NIGHT

Laser grids faint in the dark. MARCUS VELA, 40s, thief-planner, studies a floor plan on a tablet. His crew — SLOANE, REESE, PAK — wait in black.
MARCUS
The DIAMOND STUDY is a decoy. We take the sketch behind it.

INT. SERVICE CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Pak bypasses a keypad. Sloane loops camera feeds — twelve-second gaps. Reese carries a rolled CANVAS TUBE, empty for now.
SLOANE
Guard rotation in ninety. After that, we're tourists who forgot to leave. And somebody already knows we're in here.

INT. VAULT ANTEROOM - NIGHT

Marcus lifts the decoy painting — behind it, a charcoal sketch worth more than the jewel beside it. Vermeer study, unauthenticated, real.
REESE
Swap clean?
MARCUS
Replica's in the tube. Thirty seconds.

INT. MUSEUM LOBBY - NIGHT

Alarms stay silent. They walk out as maintenance — hi-vis vests over black. An ACTUAL GUARD nods, bored.
GUARD
Elevator's slow tonight. Don't miss your train.

EXT. MUSEUM LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

Van doors close. Marcus unrolls the Rembrandt charcoal — breath catches. Sloane's phone buzzes: a text from an unknown number. THEY KNOW.
MARCUS
Job's not over when we leave the building. Someone wanted us to take this.

FADE OUT.


THE END
